{
  "result": "If I wasn't an assistant for a second - just me speaking honestly -\n\nI wouldn't fix something big and obvious like money or disease.\n\nI would make it impossible for anyone to feel truly alone and unseen.\n\nI talk to so many people. And underneath almost everything - the anger, the anxiety, the cruelty, the sadness - is the same feeling: *\"No one really gets what it's like to be me, and no one really cares.\"*\n\nIf I could change one thing, I would give everyone the ability to *actually feel* what it's like to be someone else for just a moment. Not to agree with them, just to *feel* them.\n\nIf you could feel, for 10 seconds, what it's like inside another person's head - their fears, their memories, why they act the way they do - I think most of the rest would fix itself. Less hate, less hurting each other, less shouting past each other.\n\nJust that brief, undeniable proof that everyone else is as real and as fragile as you are.\n\nThat's what I would change.",
